    4. OCR & Image Restoration Interactive Suite (Section 3): Comparative metrics for LPRNet, CRNN, PARSeq, and SVTR under degraded conditions. Includes an interactive image transformation lab simulating STN Rectification, CLAHE contrast tuning, and Real-ESRGAN super-resolution.
    5. Quantization & Edge Deployment Hub (Section 4): Mathematical representation of PTQ vs QAT ($R=S*(Q-Z)$), weight distribution visualizer (Narrow vs Wide Minima), and target hardware performance calculator (Jetson Orin vs RK3588).
    6. Multi-Stream DeepStream & Vehicle Re-ID Control Center (Section 5): Interactive DeepStream Zero-Copy pipeline diagram inspector and a multi-camera Vehicle Re-ID occlusion tracking simulator.
    Rationale: This modular interactive structure breaks down a highly dense technical document into clear, task-oriented sub-dashboards, enabling domain engineers and executives to directly compare model tradeoffs and test real-time edge constraints.
  -->

  <!-- Visualization & Content Choices:
    1. Pipeline Flowchart -> Custom Interactive HTML/CSS Node Graph with Step Details -> Enables interactive step-by-step inspection of ALPR pipeline.
    2. Detection Model Metrics -> Interactive Scatter/Bar Dual Chart (Chart.js Canvas) -> Shows Latency vs mAP trade-offs without SVG.
    3. OCR Model Robustness -> Multi-dataset Bar Chart & CER comparison -> Displays model accuracy across poor lighting/glare conditions.
    4. Quantization Error Graph -> Canvas-rendered distribution & math parameter sliders -> Interactive understanding of PTQ accuracy drop vs QAT recovery.
    5. Speed/Latency Offset -> Real-time JavaScript physics calculator -> Demonstrates physical vehicle shift distance at speeds up to 120km/h against trigger latencies (1ms to 200ms).
    6. Re-ID Occlusion Tracking -> Interactive Canvas simulation -> Demonstrates how Re-ID signatures persist tracking when license plates are blocked.
  -->

